              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "The next NBA game is **Game 1 of the 2026 NBA Finals** between the **San Antonio Spurs** and the **New York Knicks**. \n\nThe game is scheduled for **Wednesday, June 3, 2026, at 8:30 p.m. ET** (7:30 p.m. local CT) and will be hosted at the **Frost Bank Center** in San Antonio, Texas.\n\nYou can purchase tickets through the following platforms:\n\n### 1. Official & Primary Tickets\n* **Ticketmaster:** As the official ticketing partner of the NBA and the San Antonio Spurs, you can find official and verified resale tickets directly on **Ticketmaster.com** or via the **official San Antonio Spurs website**. \n* *Note on Local Restrictions:* For primary (standard admission) tickets sold through the Spurs at the Frost Bank Center, there is a regional restriction requiring your billing address/zip code to be within 150 miles of the arena. If you live outside this radius, you will need to buy verified resale tickets.\n\n### 2. Secondary Resale Marketplaces\nIf you are traveling from out of town or looking for alternative seating options, major secondary marketplaces are widely available:\n* **SeatGeek**\n* **StubHub**\n* **TickPick**\n\n### Pricing and Availability Outlook\nBecause this series features the Knicks' first NBA Finals appearance since 1999, ticket demand is historically high, and prices are steep:\n* **In San Antonio (Games 1 & 2):** \"Get-in\" prices for upper-bowl seats are starting around **$1,000 to $1,300**. Lower-bowl seats are priced from $2,000 up to $47,000 for courtside VIP options.\n* **In New York (Games 3 & 4 at Madison Square Garden):** If you are looking ahead to the games in New York (starting June 8), tickets on the secondary market are significantly more expensive, with the cheapest get-in resale tickets starting between **$3,700 and $4,200**.",
